  "step_3": "The decision reason requires evaluating the least probable outcome (i.e., the most favorable outcome with the lowest probability) of each lottery and preferring the one with the more favorable value. In this case, Lottery A has a 2500€ outcome at 33%, and Lottery B has a 2400€ outcome at 34%. The least probable outcome in A is 2500€ at 33%, and in B it is 2400€ at 34%. The reason would prefer A because 2500€ > 2400€. However, the verbal report does not mention the least probable outcome at all. Instead, it evaluates a marginal change: a 1% increase in probability at the cost of 100€ less. This reflects a different reasoning process — one focused on marginal trade-offs, not on comparing the most favorable outcome in the lowest-probability scenario. Therefore, the individual did not use the decision reason. The information considered (the least probable outcomes) is not present in the report, and the justification (marginal trade-off) does not match the rule of the decision reason. Thus, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
}

